post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'
To show the boot splash:
  1. Add tinyhat-bootsplash after kms in HOOKS in /etc/mkinitcpio.conf, then run: mkinitcpio -P
  2. Add "quiet" to the kernel command line
  3. Run: systemctl enable tinyhat-bootsplash-quit.service tinyhat-bootsplash-shutdown.service
Choose or create animations with Boot Animations. Disable Plymouth if it is installed.
MSG
}
